<title>USA: First Federal Financial Q4 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>First Federal Financial Q4 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>IRONTON, Ohio 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended Sept 30.</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.06   profit	  N.A.</p>
<p> Net loss			36   profit	   $70</p>
<p>			12MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.35   profit	  N.A.</p>
<p> Net profit		   217   profit	  $353</p>
<p>	  (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: There were no shares of common stock outstanding for 1995 periods, which reflect results for First Federal Savings and Loan Association of Ironton only.</p>
<p>1996 Q4 and year periods include charge from an assessment related to deposit insurance. Earnings before the assessment totaled $142,122, or $0.23 a share, in Q4, and $394,430, or $0.64 a share, for the year.</p>
<p>Assets at Sept 30 were $56.6 million vs $51.3 million.</p>
<p>Deposits at Sept 30 were $44.8 million vs $46.2 million.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
